Access-control principles

- Public anonymous users must not access administrative audit records or retention controls.
- Enforce permissions on the server, not merely in route presentation or client behavior.
- Follow least privilege and the existing role model.
- Separate policy administration from execution authority where justified.
- Ensure ordinary content reviewers or contributors cannot administer system-wide retention unless an existing approved permission explicitly grants it.
- Record privileged policy and execution actions in the authoritative audit system.
- Avoid recursive audit events in which recording an audit event continually generates more audit events.

If the existing roles do not support a defensible separation of duties, present a precise proposed role/permission matrix for human approval.

Do not silently grant broad powers to "system_admin" or "content_manager" without checking the existing permission conventions and documenting the rationale.

